{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000209","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Explicitly labeled a “narrative review” of AI in cardiovascular pharmacovigilance. It discusses text-based surveillance and NLP, but this is a review rather than a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"“This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on AI applications... including... text-based surveillance.”"},{"record_id":"rec_000210","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Presents CLARA as a natural-language interface that executes query interpretations and asks for clarification. The abstract describes a query framework, not a primary generative text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“A natural language interface... We propose CLARA, a framework... executes them, and asks for clarification.”"},{"record_id":"rec_000211","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract frames the paper as introducing an assessment framework and mapping existing systems and benchmark resources. This is a review/framework paper, not a new primary model.","evidence_snippet":"“We map 109 agentic or agent-adjacent systems and 28 benchmark or evaluation resources... We introduce the Function--Evidence--Validation framework.”"},{"record_id":"rec_000212","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model operates on multi-omics data and evaluates on multi-omics datasets, but the abstract does not describe any substantive text or language component. It is a biological multimodal fusion paper, not a text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“Adaptive Confidence-weighted Expansion... enhance the trustworthiness of multimodal fusion models” and “four challenging multi-omics datasets.”"},{"record_id":"rec_000213","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract centers on introducing PertReasonQA as a benchmark and framework suite. Although a reference model is included, the paper is primarily a benchmark/resource contribution.","evidence_snippet":"“We introduce PertReason, a knowledge-grounded benchmark and framework suite... PertReasonQA is a benchmark.”"},{"record_id":"rec_000214","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work presents a pre-training corpus and matched evaluation suite for biology, not a new model. This is a resource paper centered on training data and evaluation.","evidence_snippet":"“We present TheBioCollection, a 52.6B-token pre-training-scale corpus” and “TheBioCollection-Eval.”"},{"record_id":"rec_000215","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SpaCellAgent automates analysis and narrative generation with an LLM multi-agent workflow. The abstract describes orchestration over existing tools, which fits an application wrapper rather than a primary text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“an autonomous large language model (LLM) multi-agent framework that automates end-to-end spatiotemporal analysis and narrative generation.”"},{"record_id":"rec_000216","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is explicitly a scoping review of AI in genomic science. It summarizes prior studies and methods rather than introducing a new primary model.","evidence_snippet":"“We conducted a PRISMA-ScR scoping review... Eligible studies applied AI to genomics or closely allied omics.”"}]}
